MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_001: Hey, Fabio. Do you have a second?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_002: A second, perhaps. But that is all I can afford. Please\nbe quick.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_003: Can you ease up for once? Anyway, I want you\nto tell me about the caves, and the phantoms.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_004: Certainly not. And why should I? Is this\ninformation of any use to you?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_005: Let me spell it out. We're allies. We're working\ntogether. So enough games!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_006: An assertion so irrelevant I cannot credit it. If\nDietrich is not concerned, why are you?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_007: That's exactly why! We have no idea what you're up\nto. How do I know you're not just using us?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_008: As long as he gets to fight, Sweetie's happy. So it's\nup to me to protect him!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_009: Protect Dietrich? You? Still, you are strong, and I\nsuppose I ought to acknowledge that.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_010: Darn right you should! So what's the story? Spill!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_011: Yet even so, you are a barbarian! Take your clumsy\nattempt to shove that door...
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_012: That's...how doors work? You push them. And then\nthey open. That's doors!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_013: Like my dad always said, where there's a will,\nthere's a way.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_014: A door such as that will not be moved by a simple\napplication of force.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_015: Even the Crest of Blaiddyd could not help you.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_016: No, no... Better to not waste my time. Your behavior\nis simply too like a beast.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_017: To identify food you have never encountered before,\nyou sniff it—lick it, even... Like an animal!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_018: Are you kidding? How else are you supposed to tell\nif it's safe to eat? That's just normal!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_019: You sure do like to call people "beasts." Does that\ninclude Sweetie?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_020: Well...yes. But he is special. I have never seen\na beast of such unparalleled beauty.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_021: You sure do like to throw "beast" around! But why\nme? What makes me different from Sweetie?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_022: Dietrich is special. Must I list the ways you differ?\nThey are too numerous.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_023: You requested a second. And as I predicted, you\nhave wasted much more of my time. Farewell.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_C_024: This guy! What a clump of rotting seaweed. Is this\nnormal in Fódlan?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_001: Gah... What an infestation of foes. We may well\nbe outmatched.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_002: Fabio! Look out! Hya-AAH!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_003: Oh. It's quiet. That's the last of them.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_004: To think that a creature like you would come to\nmy rescue...
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_005: Ehehe. Good thing I kept an eye out. Look at you!\nYou're about done for the day.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_006: Well, you made it, and that's what counts. Now show\nme your arm. Oof, that looks bad.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_007: I don't know what you're talking about!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_008: I can smell the blood on you. It...doesn't smell right.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_009: Now stop being a baby and give it here. I'll take\ncare of it.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_010: Entrust my body's maintenance to you? No, thank\nyou. I have no wish to deteriorate further.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_011: Will you just shut up and do what I tell you?\nCome here!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_012: Unhand me! This instant! How dare you!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_013: Agh. I knew it. This is bad. Now would you\nkeep still?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_014: You are more skilled than I anticipated. I feared you\nmight wound me further. It seems not.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_015: {SetColor=Gray}Wound you further? I should wound you further!\nDoes he ever shut— Hm?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_016: Your skin is DRY. Dry like a-dried-out-lake-bed-\nunder-the-hot-sun dry!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_017: Well, might as well finish what I started. Here. This\nwill help your skin.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_018: What is this malodorous sludge? It has an unpleasant\nsheen! Desist!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_019: Balm made out of sea-beast blubber and herbs.\nAnd don't say another nasty word. I'm helping you!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_020: OK, that'll do it. It's wrapped up nice and tight, so\nyou should be able to use your arm.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_021: You must understand I would not do the same for\nyou... So why do you aid me?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_022: Not that I expected better from you, but why not just\nsay "thank you" instead of asking a dumb question?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_023: I guess I'll answer. Two reasons. First, unlike you,\nI'm a nice person.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_024: Second, because Sweetie sees something in you.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_025: Ah...
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_026: Honestly, that's really the only reason. I can't\nstand you.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_027: But you're our ally. So it makes sense to help you.\nDoesn't it?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_028: I see... Meddlesome as well as arrogant, this beast.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_029: Eugh...
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_030: {SetColor=Gray}Hm? I already perceive an improvement! Could it\nbe...this accursed balm?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_031: I see that the creepy mumbling is back.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_032: Oh... I... I simply had the realization that even a\nbeast may be wise. Esmeralda, I thank you.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_033: Did... Did you just say "thank you"? Now that it\nfinally happened... I don't know if I want it!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_034: How dare you! I only did so because you demanded\nit of me! You should be thanking me!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_035: Wait. I should be thanking YOU for thanking me?\nHow does that make sense?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_B_036: Can't win 'em all, I guess. Well, at least he's\ndoing better.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_001: Why did you tag along? I've been hunting sea beasts\nsince I was a kid. I'm fine on my own.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_002: Is it not obvious? I am loathe to fall even deeper into\nyour debt.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_003: Debt? What do you mean? I just wanted some\nsea-beast jerky.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_004: You ought not to lie if you have no skill for it.\nYou are making balm from the blubber. For me.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_005: What? No! I'm making it for myself! I just give you\nmy leftovers!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_006: Another transparent lie. You must know my supply\nof balm is nearly depleted. Otherwise, why now?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_007: Well...since you started using it...you've been\nlooking better.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_008: But if a beast's help isn't good enough for you, just\nforget it.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_009: I said no such thing. What I am saying is that it is\nonly right I shoulder my part of the burden.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_010: Wait. Say that again?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_011: I will not repeat myself, so listen closely. I require\nyour balm, so I offer my aid.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_012: Fabio? Did you hit your head?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_013: How rude! Cast you into the sea, shall I?
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_014: It's just... You're not the kind of guy to think about\nanybody else's feelings. Ever. Not once.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_015: I will admit as much. But my understanding\nhas undergone a change.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_016: As I have observed Dietrich, and you, I have come\nto understand your natures.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_017: Take you. You may have no learning whatsoever, but\nyour heart is a sympathetic one. That is estimable.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_018: Take you. You may have no learning whatsoever, but\nyou are sympathetic. That is, in its essence, human.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_019: You don't know how to hold back, but... For you, that\nwas extremely nice. Thanks, I guess. Ehehe!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_020: And if you're going to be nice for once, I'll pay it\nback. Here. It's a talisman.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_021: A useless talisman carved from sea-beast bone, in the\nshape of a warrior. A superstitious trinket. I accept.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_022: No! I changed my mind! Give it back! It's not for\nyou! It's for Sweetie!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_023: What? This piece of refuse? Absolutely not! I am\nconfiscating this!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_024: So rude! I'm Sweetie's future bride, I'll have\nyou know!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_025: How droll. No, it is I who has claimed a spot at his\nside. You can continue your journey—alone!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_026: Me? I think it's YOU who should get lost! I'm with\nSweetie, and that's final! Go away!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_027: I think not, you odious beast! Dietrich and I shall\nnever be parted!
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_028: Fine, fine. Come on, it's time to head back.\nSweetie is waiting.
MID_SE_Fab_Esm_A_029: Very well. It is best we not keep him. On this one\nthing, we are in accord.